#33757
"The Throne Room of Death"
"You stand in a room with all dark appearance of a gothic cathedral built in
epic proportions.  Large stone slabs form the bricks of the walls and ornately
carved pillars rise up to meet the vaulted ceiling.  An otherworldly light
suffuses the place allowing you to see without any hint of the light source
yet shadows seem to lurk in every corner.  There are no windows here and no
other exits save the one you came in by.  A raised dais set into the north
wall provides the only break in the contour of the floor with a black carpet
lined in embroidered lilies leading up to stop just short of it.  Above the
dais, hanging suspended in mid-air several feet above the floor is the God of
Death himself.
"
""
